<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anwar Sadat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1981">1981</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anwar Sadat was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 1970 until his assassination in 1981. He launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yom-kippur-war">October War</a> of 1973 against Israel, opened the economy and turned Egypt from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. He signed the Camp <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Accords and the peace treaty of 1979 with Israel, for which he shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat.jpg" alt="Anwar Sadat" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anwar_Sadat_cropped_(cropped)(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Anwar Sadat</b>, president from 1970, renamed the state the Arab Republic of Egypt in 1971 and made Islam the official religion and Sharia the principal source of legislation.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-egypt">Republic of Egypt · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>149 made &quot;Bilādī, Bilādī, Bilādī&quot; the national anthem, in an arrangement by the musician Mohamed Abdel Wahab made at the direction of President <b>Anwar Sadat</b>.</blockquote><a href="/songs/biladi-biladi-biladi">Biladi, Biladi, Biladi</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1979, during the peace negotiations with Israel, President <b>Anwar Sadat</b> replaced it with the less militant &quot;Bilady, Bilady, Bilady&quot;, which remains Egypt's national anthem.</blockquote><a href="/songs/wallah-zaman-ya-silahi">Wallah Zaman, Ya Silahi</a></li><li><blockquote>At the White House, <b>Anwar Sadat</b> and Menachem Begin signed the first peace treaty between Israel and an Arab state, building on the Camp David Accords.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-26">26 March in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Egypt's president <b>Anwar Sadat</b> flew to Israel and the next day addressed the Knesset in Jerusalem.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-19">19 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Islamist army officers shot <b>Anwar Sadat</b> during a military parade in Cairo marking the 1973 war.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-6">6 October in history</a></li></ul></section>
